{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1527092-madness-condition-inconsistencies","id":1527092,"title":"Madness - Condition Inconsistencies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-19T15:10:57-08:00","id":1527092,"title":"Madness - Condition Inconsistencies","content":"Edit - this is in reference to Obsession, not Madness. Just noted that in CoD and HTV 2e rule books, the Condition 'Obsession' indicates players enjoy the 10-again quality on all rolls related to their obsession. But isn't that the default anyways?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in the VTR, MTA, CTL etc. books, the Obsession Condition imparts the <b>9-again</b> quality on all rolls related to the obsession. Which would seem to make more sense.<br /> <br /> This isn't the only inconsistency I've found between conditions, tilts, merits, etc. which you'd think would be standardized across the books. Seems Onyx Path would greatly benefit from someone doing a pass on these kinds of things prior to printing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27475,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27475-burzghash","user":"Burzghash","date":". 12-22-2023, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27475-burzghash","name":"Burzghash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-19T18:56:23-08:00","id":1527103,"title":"","content":"The pass is that the book's advance copy is put out for a couple of weeks with an errata collection form, and corrections are then made to the final draft. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1485789-hunter-2nd-edition-errata\">You should already know this.</a><br /> <br /> Speaking of inconsistencies, you're describing the <b>Obsession</b> Condition here, not the Madness Condition, which has its own issues (chiefly semantic) but doesn't mess with what dice results explode into additional dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-19T20:02:03-08:00","id":1527106,"title":"","content":"You mean it's almost like the different games are entirely different games? That maybe some things are more thematic for one game than the other and so will be more or less powerful or easier or harder to gain than in a different game? That's a feature, not a flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-20T07:36:00-08:00","id":1527119,"title":"","content":"I think the answer is that Conditions <i>are</i> standardised; it's just that there were <i>two</i> different cores, and therefore two different standards (one of which is possibly wrong). Requiem, Awakening, and Lost use the Condition from <i>God-Machine Chronicles</i>. Vigil uses the Condition from the <i>CofD</i> core.<br /> <br /> The way the Condition is written in the core makes me think that it was intended to be a straight rewrite of the one in GMC, but they got the values wrong. (Interestingly I've been using an earlier pdf of the core and it's version of <i>Obsession</i> has both values as 9, which makes the writing more obviously odd.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T11:02:04-08:00","id":1527250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1527092-madness-condition-inconsistencies?p=1527106#post1527106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean it's almost like the different games are entirely different games? That maybe some things are more thematic for one game than the other and so will be more or less powerful or easier or harder to gain than in a different game? That's a feature, not a flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>lol, so different games have a condition which applies the 10-again rule (which is the default anyways) whereas others have rules that actually make sense and cause a condition different from what is the default anyways?<br /> <br /> lol, yeah, you clearly thought this through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27475-burzghash","name":"Burzghash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T11:03:10-08:00","id":1527251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1527092-madness-condition-inconsistencies?p=1527106#post1527106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean it's almost like the different games are entirely different games? That maybe some things are more thematic for one game than the other and so will be more or less powerful or easier or harder to gain than in a different game? That's a feature, not a flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! The other thing I like is how they apparently realized that 'crippled' is not the appropriate terminology and swapped it out for 'disabled' in virtually every other game line... and then because whoever was doing HTV literally just did a shitty copy-paste job, it's back to being 'crippled' again in that book.<br /> <br /> But I'm sure that's also just a case of &quot;different games are different&quot;, am I rite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27475,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27475-burzghash","user":"Burzghash","date":". 12-22-2023, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27475-burzghash","name":"Burzghash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T11:05:37-08:00","id":1527252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1527092-madness-condition-inconsistencies?p=1527103#post1527103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The pass is that the book's advance copy is put out for a couple of weeks with an errata collection form, and corrections are then made to the final draft. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1485789-hunter-2nd-edition-errata\">You should already know this.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm aware that they have this process, and that it's also done equally incompetently as far as consistency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1527092-madness-condition-inconsistencies?p=1527103#post1527103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of inconsistencies, you're describing the <b>Obsession</b> Condition here, not the Madness Condition, which has its own issues (chiefly semantic) but doesn't mess with what dice results explode into additional dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong. Which dice are exploded depends on which book you're reading. Again, because of consistency issues.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/2B38XGr\" target=\"_blank\">https://imgur.com/2B38XGr</a><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://imgur.com/2B38XGr\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://imgur.com/2B38XGr\" data-thumb-url=\"https://imgur.com/2B38XGr\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27475,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27475-burzghash","user":"Burzghash","date":". 12-22-2023, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27475-burzghash","name":"Burzghash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T11:12:33-08:00","id":1527253,"title":"","content":"By the way in case Onyx Path happens across this - I'd be perfectly willing to help with your poor cross-gameline consistency as a consultant. Just saying \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2642\ufe0f","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27475-burzghash","name":"Burzghash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T12:10:28-08:00","id":1527257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Burzghash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1527092-madness-condition-inconsistencies?p=1527252#post1527252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am saying that the Madness Condition, which you named in the thread title and referred to in the OP before you corrected it, does not have any listed inconsistencies between books. I am not contesting that there is an inconsistency with the Obsession Condition as listed between books.<br /> <br /> Did you have any useful purpose in making this thread on the forums instead of leaving a review on the book's store page describing your issue, or did you just swing back around after taking a ten month gap year to be smarmy in the exact same way you were in another thread you made on the same topic over a year ago?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T12:15:19-08:00","id":1527258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1527092-madness-condition-inconsistencies?p=1527257#post1527257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you have any useful purpose in making this thread on the forums instead of leaving a review on the book's store page describing your issue, or did you just swing back around after taking a ten month gap year to be smarmy in the exact same way you were in another thread you made on the same topic over a year ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, just here to clarify if I was misreading something or if OP is just amateur in their publishing capacity.<br /> <br /> Thanks for confirming both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27475-burzghash","name":"Burzghash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T12:48:06-08:00","id":1527261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Burzghash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1527092-madness-condition-inconsistencies?p=1527253#post1527253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way in case Onyx Path happens across this - I'd be perfectly willing to help with your poor cross-gameline consistency as a consultant. Just saying \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2642\ufe0f</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that my copy of the COFD book doesn't have the issue you're talking about and that even you admit it is correct across most of the thousands of pages of text, meanwhile you couldn't get 100 words right between the post and the title, I doubt they need your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-22T15:33:01-08:00","id":1527275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Burzghash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1527092-madness-condition-inconsistencies?p=1527250#post1527250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> lol, so different games have a condition which applies the 10-again rule (which is the default anyways) whereas others have rules that actually make sense and cause a condition different from what is the default anyways?<br /> <br /> lol, yeah, you clearly thought this through.</div> </div> </div> </div>A possible reason for a Condition to give the 10-again rule would be to help play around with effects that take it away. If you're not under any of those effects this version of Obsession wouldn't do anything, but depending on how stacking rules set the order effects are applied in it might end up with you losing 10-again but regaining it for certain actions.<br /> <br /> It's a niche thing that even if it works is unlikely to regularly come up, but it's still a valid (and for the kind of people who become imbued thematic) way to interpret how such a Condition might work.<br /> <br /> Is it intentionally written that way? Who knows, CofD mostly tries to avoid stacking effects but it's certainly possible someone decided it made more sense as a counter than a buff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-23T02:40:46-08:00","id":1527294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1527092-madness-condition-inconsistencies?p=1527261#post1527261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-righ